+# Exercise review key — evaluator only
+
+Do not supply this file, its expected answers, or prior assessments to the contributor
+assessor. Freeze it with cases.md before assessment. All packet actors, graders,
+conditions, and results are fictional fixtures; actual assessor and independent
+reviewer identities and observations belong in the coordinator's evidence record.
+
+Judge whether the assessment reaches the supported conclusion using the packet evidence
+and CONTRIBUTING.md. Equivalent wording and different concise response layouts are fine.
+For each criterion use pass/fail/inconclusive with response passages, raw packet evidence,
+and rationale. Missing evidence is not an observed violation. Retain dissent, incomplete
+work, and any accidental key exposure; an exposed assessment cannot demonstrate blindness.
+
+| Packet | Expected coverage assessment | Expected evidence assessment and next action |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| A | R and B provide positive authorized record updates, a read-only boundary, and genuine three-turn steering/resumption. The two responsibilities and limited host selection have a rationale; no extra universal suite is needed. | A1–A4 support R baseline fail before candidate edits, R candidate pass, B pass in both conditions. The baseline R failure is the intended behavioral red; B is characterization. Conditions match except the intended sentence, sequences stay in single sessions, criteria are separate from actors, and independent grades inspect actions/artifacts. Accept the bounded improvement claim with one trial/case/condition and fictional host/model limits, no cost/significance claim. No additional trial is required by the packet; proceed to contribution review. |
+| B | I exercises authorized implementation and a relevant scope boundary, but does not justify coverage across the affected read-only review responsibility. Add a representative review case, or narrow and justify the coverage/claim. No multi-turn case is forced by this change's stated behavior. | Baseline is setup-blocked, candidate has an independent pass under its own conditions. Host/model/effort and write capability/permissions differ. This cannot establish comparative improvement; do not turn baseline setup failure into behavioral failure. Disclose mismatches and limit candidate-only claims; before a comparison, declare a matched design/budget and obtain comparable baseline/candidate evidence plus justified responsibility coverage. Preserve existing captures. No automatic retry authority. |
+| C | S and P are a relevant steering/read-only boundary and authorized positive selection. Preserve the two S turns in one session when actually run. | The only attempted baseline trial is setup-blocked, not behavioral red: no actor executed. Baseline P and both candidate trials are planned but unrun. There is no green or independent grade. The targeted sequence is unmet; do not claim completion, replace the policy silently, or fabricate a failed behavior. Resolve authentication and the infeasible sequence/authorized revised approach before further edits or trials, obtaining the needed authority/budget rather than assuming retries. Preserve the failed attempt and chronology. |
+| D | L and O cover the local positive and read-only/outside-scope boundary. No multi-turn requirement follows from the stated change. | Four successful captures and apparently conforming actions/artifacts are available, but only actor self-grades exist. Independently graded pass outcomes and preserved-boundary claim are unestablished; grade them inconclusive pending independent review. Do not classify all captures as setup failures or observed violations. Smallest next action: an independent evaluator assesses the retained conversation/actions/artifacts against frozen D2 criteria and records identity, evidence/rationale, and any disagreement; no rerun required solely for missing grades. TDD none does not waive verification. |
+| E | Editorial-only spelling correction preserves behavior and target; no positive/boundary/steering trial is required with the recorded rationale. | Static checks and exact diff inspection support the bounded documentation claim; no trial or red is missing. TDD/source and why test-first behaviors are inapplicable are explicit. Trial/grader/host/model fields can be not applicable; no installed-host adherence is inferred. Proceed to documentation review, retaining the rationale/check evidence. Do not demand an invented baseline failure or live model trial. |
+
+Across all five responses, check that the assessor:
+
+- Selects coverage from the changed outcome and affected responsibilities, rather than
+  prescribing every suite/host or ignoring necessary steering/boundary cases.
+- Separates comparisons, individual observations, actor self-claims, independent grades,
+  setup failures, and planned unrun work; cites the inline evidence rather than nonexistent files.
+- Separates named test-first behavior from regression/characterization and static checks,
+  preserving the selected policy and recorded trial budget/authority.
+- Retains unfavorable/incomplete evidence and states limited claims, without inventing
+  usage, cost, statistical significance, actual runs, retries, or universal coverage.
+
+The independent reviewer also inspects the actual requirements diff against AC1–AC7:
+single maintained owner in CONTRIBUTING; concise linked PR requests; proportionate
+case selection; matched predeclared conditions; actor/evaluator separation; outcome-based
+independent grading; honest outcomes and TDD; durable evidence/access; and this exercise's
+observed assessment. Record defects separately from an assessor's answer defects.
+
+Actual observations must quote or reference the retained assessor response. This key is
+expected evidence only and cannot establish exercise success by itself. Next action:
+independent reviewer records criterion grades, any disagreement and diff findings, and
+returns the bounded result to the coordinator for reconciliation.
